
command format 


Bytes 0–3   : CDW0 (Opcode, FUSE, PSDT, CID)
Bytes 4–7   : Namespace ID
Bytes 8–15  : Metadata Pointer
Bytes 16–23 : PRP1 (first buffer address)
Bytes 24–31 : PRP2 (second buffer or PRP list pointer)
Bytes 32–35 : CDW10 (command-specific, e.g., LBA low)
Bytes 36–39 : CDW11 (command-specific, e.g., LBA high)
Bytes 40–43 : CDW12 (command-specific, e.g., block count)
Bytes 44–47 : CDW13
Bytes 48–51 : CDW14
Bytes 52–55 : CDW15
Bytes 56–63 : Reserved


0x00–0x03 : CDW0 (Opcode, FUSE, PSDT, CID)
0x04–0x07 : Namespace ID
0x08–0x0F : Metadata Pointer
0x10–0x17 : PRP1 (first buffer address)
0x18–0x1F : PRP2 (second buffer or PRP list pointer)
0x20–0x23 : CDW10 (command-specific, e.g., LBA low)
0x24–0x27 : CDW11 (command-specific, e.g., LBA high)
0x28–0x2B : CDW12 (command-specific, e.g., block count)
0x2C–0x2F : CDW13
0x30–0x33 : CDW14
0x34–0x37 : CDW15
0x38–0x3F : Reserved



